      "id": "jsonl-summary-feature",
      "prompt": "Implement a JSONL summarization CLI. Input is strict UTF-8 without BOM. Each LF-terminated or final unterminated nonblank line is one record; CRLF is one line break, while a lone CR is whitespace within a line and never a record delimiter. Empty input and lines containing only ASCII space, tab, form-feed, carriage return, or LF emit no output and succeed; CRLF is one line break, and a lone CR is whitespace. Every record must be an object with exactly string category and finite safe-integer numeric amount; categories must be Unicode scalar-value strings (no lone surrogates); null, booleans, scalars, arrays, duplicate keys after JSON unescaping, missing or extra keys, and non-finite or unsafe amounts are malformed. Group with collision-safe storage by exact Unicode code-point category order, sum only safe integers, and serialize each group as exactly one compact Node JSON.stringify-compatible JSON object `{\"category\":<JSON string>,\"amount\":<integer>}` followed by LF, with category first. On malformed JSONL, write exactly `invalid JSONL at line <n>\\n` to stderr, where n is the earliest malformed input line; write no stdout, and exit 1.",
